Subject: [PATCH] drm/panfrost: Initialize MMU interrupts during probe

The GPU reset leaves MMU interrupts masked. Runtime resume currently
initializes the MMU, but a kernel without CONFIG_PM never takes that
path. A growable tiler heap then stalls on an unhandled MMU fault.

Clear pending faults and enable MMU interrupts after installing the
threaded handler so first use does not depend on a runtime resume.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
@@ -909,5 +909,7 @@ int panfrost_mmu_init(struct panfrost_device *pfdev)
 		return err;
 	}
 
+	panfrost_mmu_reset(pfdev);
+
 	return 0;
 }
